! ======================================================================
! test_v0983_h2o_b3lyp_rijk_optfreq -- analytical RI-JK gradient:
! hybrid optimization + semi-numerical frequencies on the fitted
! J+K surface.
!
! Water B3LYP/6-31G(d), %ri jk (def2-universal-JKFIT).
!
! Reference (v0.98.3, 1 thread, reference BLAS):
!   Final energy:  -76.375645001339   (4 optimizer steps)
!   Modes:  1695.91 / 3718.38 / 3845.09 cm^-1
! Conventional opt+freq, same route (%hess_method numerical):
!   -76.375622656920; 1695.87 / 3718.46 / 3845.23 cm^-1
!   -> optimum offset -22.3 uHa (7.4 uHa/atom); frequencies within
!      0.04-0.14 cm^-1.  FD validation of the analytic gradient
!      against RI-JK energies: 6.9e-8 (HF, pure-K case), 8e-8
!      (B3LYP), 3.1e-7 (UKS B3LYP; per-spin -c_HF/2 factors).
! ======================================================================
%method  B3LYP
%basis   6-31gd
%job     opt+freq
%ri      jk
%charge  0
%mult    1
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
